WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.390
You all know that I don't subscribe to the
polling conspiracy theories that you can't

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.779
trust polls that polling is fake.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:12.820
That polling is somebody in an office making
up numbers that the polls only call old people

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:13.820
on landlines.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.359
I don't subscribe to any of those conspiracy
theories because they're bogus.

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:20.300
And we know that they're bogus by looking
at methodology.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.880
Well done polling, especially when you average
a bunch of good polls.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.580
You get a really good sense of where races
look at 2016.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.360
Hillary was leading the national polls by
3.2.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.390
She won by 2.1.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.440
That's within the margin of error that the
polls were correct nationally in 2016.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:46.610
Now, something really dishonest was done by
CNN last week with a poll that they did.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.140
And I want to call it out.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:54.610
CNN announced that in battleground states,
Trump is winning 52 to 45.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:59.160
Now, as a savvy news consumer, you should
immediately say, what?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.320
What does that mean?

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.489
Fifty two to forty five across battleground
states.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:10.749
Are you saying that you added up all of the
different people in those states and in total,

00:01:10.749 --> 00:01:12.259
Trump is winning by seven?

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:16.329
Do you mean that his average lead in each
state is seven?

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:20.280
Are you waiting those results for the populations
of the.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.280
What does that mean?

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.719
Because states are different populations,
different electoral vote values?

00:01:24.719 --> 00:01:31.240
Well, if you look at page nine of the CNN
poll, the methodology page actually says for

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.560
the subset of five hundred and eighty three
adults living in the 15 battleground states,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.080
there is a margin of error of 5.3 percentage
points.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:46.279
So, first of all, you've got to sample that
across 15 different battleground states is

00:01:46.279 --> 00:01:48.600
only five hundred and eighty three people
total.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.850
Now, that could be thirty eight people for
state.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.450
Not a good sample size.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:58.359
Some states maybe had more of that sample
and some less because of their population

00:01:58.359 --> 00:02:00.119
and the margin of error is 5.3.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:04.119
So this could be essentially a tie or Trump
could be leading by 12.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:05.600
This tells us very little.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:11.220
But the most important thing is that this
poll, when it says Trump's winning in these

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:18.160
15 states by seven, it doesn't tell us how
far ahead Trump or Biden are in any particular

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.160
state.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.300
What I mean is Georgia's included in these
15 states.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.420
Well, Trump's winning by Georgia by at around
8:00 right now, 7 or 8, is Georgia even really

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.530
a battleground?

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.830
Georgia has 16 electoral votes.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.280
It's not really in play for Joe Biden.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.390
Why is it included and how is it skewing these
results?

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:41.800
Some other states that are included are actual
battleground states like, for example, Nevada.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.800
It's actually sort of close.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.080
Biden is plus four.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.780
But Nevada only has six electoral votes.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.830
So how are you waiting these different states?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:56.470
And what does it mean that Trump is winning
by seven across the states?

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.470
This poll doesn't have very useful information.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.980
And unfortunately, it was picked up on by
a bunch of right wing media and even some

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:04.980
left wing media.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.400
And it is being spread like some kind of gospel.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.490
So let's do something that makes more sense.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:15.490
Let's look at each state one by one and then
total up the electoral vote.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.760
So when you actually break this down, Joe
Biden is winning Arizona, Colorado, Florida,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:28.530
Maine, Michigan, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire,
New Mexico, Pennsylvania, Virginia, Wisconsin.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:33.910
And then on the other hand, Donald Trump is
winning in Georgia.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.350
Donald Trump is winning in North Carolina.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:42.900
In Ohio, the point is, when you add up the
electoral votes in these supposed battleground

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:49.040
states, regardless of the combined population,
as of right now, Joe Biden would get close

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.750
to 75 percent of the electoral votes from
these 15 battleground states.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.470
Now, I want to be really clear.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.470
This is just a snapshot.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:58.270
It's a moment in time.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.610
This is not about Biden's got this.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.070
It's not about staying home in November.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.260
It's not about Biden's going to win.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:11.920
The point is, when I simply say Trump's winning
by seven in these 15 battleground states,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.750
you then look at each state, you see, wait
a second, Biden's winning most of the states

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.440
and most of the electoral votes right now.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.370
So polling is valuable in two ways.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.431
And this isn't either of them.

00:04:21.431 --> 00:04:28.090
Polling is valuable to be able to say what
is one state look like or polling is valuable

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:34.090
to say, what is the national popular vote
looking like, giving us what seems to be a

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:39.520
blended popular vote for fifteen states where
you call them battlegrounds.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.030
But some, like Georgia, are not considered
battleground states.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.040
It is deceptive.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.290
It tells us nothing.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:51.960
And it actually fuels uncritical reporting
from left, right and center media outlets.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.960
That only confuses people even more.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.040
Let's not fall for it.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.530
That's why it's important to understand what
was done here.

